{"name":"Sea Cliff","hex":"#a5c7df","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sea Cliff","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place in the United States:\nA neighbourhood on the west side of San Francisco, California.\nAn unincorporated community in Ventura County, California.\nA village in the town of Oyster Bay, Nassau County, New York.","A neighbourhood on the west side of San Francisco, California."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sea_Cliff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seacliff, South Australia","blocks":[{"text":"Seacliff is a coastal suburb located in the capital city of South Australia; Adelaide. Overseen by the council, City of Holdfast Bay, this suburb is adjacent to South Brighton, Seacliff Park, Marino and Kingston Park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Seacliff_Beach.jpg/330px-Seacliff_Beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seacliff%2C_South_Australia"},{"title":"Seacliff Park, South Australia","blocks":[{"text":"Seacliff Park is a suburb of Adelaide partly in the City of Marion and the City of Holdfast Bay. The suburb is adjacent to South Brighton in the north, Seaview Downs to the east, Hallett Cove to the south, and Marino and Seacliff on the west. The suburb is divided diagonally by Ocean Road, with the northern part of the suburb mainly residential, and the southern park partly occupied by a golf course and a quarry."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seacliff_Park%2C_South_Australia"},{"title":"Cliffed coast","blocks":[{"text":"A cliffed coast, also called an abrasion coast, is a form of coast where the action of marine waves has formed steep cliffs that may or may not be precipitous. It contrasts with a flat or alluvial coast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Cliffed_coast_%28shematic_view%29.svg/330px-Cliffed_coast_%28shematic_view%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cliffed_coast"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG/500px-Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG/1280px-Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG/500px-Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crags on the southwestern coast of Portugal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKlippenk%C3%BCste.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/The_cliff-top%2C_hilly_suburb_of_Dover_Heights_%28Sydney%2C_Australia%29.png/500px-The_cliff-top%2C_hilly_suburb_of_Dover_Heights_%28Sydney%2C_Australia%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/The_cliff-top%2C_hilly_suburb_of_Dover_Heights_%28Sydney%2C_Australia%29.png/500px-The_cliff-top%2C_hilly_suburb_of_Dover_Heights_%28Sydney%2C_Australia%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb